%constbyteintegerarray document control(0 : 15) =    %c
no, no, yes, no, yes, no, no, no, no, no, no,
no, no, no, yes, no
!* THE ABOVE ARRAY DEFINES FOR EACH DEVICE TYPE WHEN BEING ACCESSED
!* AS AN INPUT DEVICE WHETHER DOCUMENT CONTROL INFORMATION IS AVAILABLE
!* IF IT IS NOT THE DATA BEING INPUT IS JUST PUT IN THE DEFAULT QUEUE
!* ASSOCIATED WITH THAT INPUT DEVICE. IT MAY SEEM RATHER
!* WEIRD FOR A LINE PRINTER TO BE AN INPUT DEVICE BUT THAT IS THE
!* TYPE OF DEVICE SPOOLR IS PRETENDING TO BE. I.E. A REMOTE PRINTER FOR
!* ANOTHER PROCESSOR.
!*
!* Modification of this was made in Feb. '88.
!* From this point on a 'DO' (type 10) input stream is expected to have
!* a complete document descriptor as the first data received. In this way
!* the stream is used for transfer of complete documents and their descriptors
!* between EMAS systems.  Here then no CONTROL is expected as such (i.e. 
!* //DOC..).

%conststring (12) %array header type(1 : 4) =     %c
"Line Printer", "Paper Tape", "Card Punch", "Doc Transfer"
%constbyteintegerarray trailer overhead(1:3) = %c
12, 200, 1
